d the MES application.The issue is resolved now.\", \"Closed Date\": \"2026-02-24\", \"R&D Tickets\": \"FNP-1013\", \"Start time \": \"2026-02-23 23:48:00\", \"Account Name\": \"National Gypsum Company\", \"Product Line\": \"FactoryEye\", \"Resolved by \": \"\", \"Shift Manager\": \"Vibha Khanke\", \"Downtime(Mins)\": \"132\", \"SF case Number\": \"00116351\", \"Internal Status\": \"Closed\", \"Date/Time Closed\": \"2026-02-24 19:07:00\", \"Date/Time Opened\": \"2026-02-23 23:48:00\", \"Alert Description\": \"NGC - CIN MES showing no communication\", \"Incident Report status\": \"Yes\", \"Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)\": \"5\", \"More Details about resolution\": \"we have restarted the MES application.The issue is resolved now.\"}, \"unmapped\": {\"More Details about resolution\": \"we have restarted the MES application.The issue is resolved now.\"}, \"source_row\": 205, \"excel_serials\": {\"End Time\": \"46077.796527777777\", \"Closed Date\": \"46077\", \"Start time \": \"46076.991666666669\", \"Date/Time Closed\": \"46077.796527777777\", \"Date/Time Opened\": \"46076.991666666669\"}}',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-30 12:38:15','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(595,'INC-211',NULL,'SMC Production Incident – Project Execution Stuck Due to High Log/Data Storage','Multiple projects running in the SMC Production environment entered a stuck execution state.\n\nThe issue was initially identified when Health Check alerts were triggered because the Health Check project, which continuously reports production metrics, also became stuck. As a result, no monitoring metrics were generated, indicating a broader issue affecting project execution.\n\nDuring the investigation, it was observed that several project messages remained in a pending state and were no longer being processed.\n\nTo restore normal production processing, the affected projects were redeployed, additional projects that were in a stuck execution state were restarted, and project execution resumed successfully.','critical','closed',2,'Babai Chatterjee',2,'SMC',13,'All Projects',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,'[{\"type\": \"comment\", \"action\": \"commented\", \"author\": \"Babai Chatterjee\", \"detail\": \"This issue is temporararily resolved by redeploying affected projects.\", \"author_id\": 2, \"created_at\": \"2026-08-05T10:07:11.714Z\"}]','2026-08-03 23:56','2026-08-03 23:56:00','2026-08-04 03:56:00.000000','2026-08-04 02:00','2026-08-04 02:00:00','2026-08-04 06:00:00.000000','2026-08-04','EST','America/New_York',0,30,30,'30m','To identify the cause of the issue, the following investigation activities were performed:\n•	Verified the pending messages for the affected projects. \n•	Reviewed the execution status of running projects. \n•	Analyzed project storage utilization under the production project directory. \n•	Performed filesystem utilization analysis using df -h. \n•	Performed project-level storage analysis using du -sh. \n•	Conducted folder-level analysis for projects consuming high disk space.\n\nFilesystem	Total Size	Used	Available	Usage\n/dev/nvme0n1p1	200 GB	99 GB	101 GB	50%\n\nObservation\nThe production server had approximately 101 GB of available disk space. Therefore, the issue was not caused by overall server disk exhaustion.\nProject-level storage analysis identified the following storage utilization:\n•	MX_Peru: 38 GB – The logs directory alone occupied approximately 38 GB, while the other folders were relatively small. \n•	MX_Bolivia: 30 GB – Large storage consumption was observed primarily within the project logs. \n•	MX_Colombia: 16 GB. \n•	Netherlands: 8 GB. \n•	Brazil: 3.9 GB – The data directory consumed more than 1 GB of storage. \n•	Other projects: Less than 1 GB each. \n\nThese observations indicate that a significant amount of storage was being consumed by project-generated logs and accumulated project data.','To restore normal production processing, the following actions were performed:\n\n•	Redeployed the following projects: \no	MX_Peru \no	MX_Bolivia \no	Brazil \n\n•	Restarted additional projects that were in a stuck execution state. \n\n•	Verified that project execution resumed successfully after redeployment and restarts. \n          These actions resolved the issue temporarily and allowed production processing to continue.','By OC Team','00135911',NULL,'15m',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2h 4m',124,'2026-08-05 09:57:08','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(598,'INC-212',NULL,'SMC - Local Agent Connectors not running for last 10 minutes','We have received critical alert - SMC - Local Agent Connectors not running for last 10 minutes.','critical','closed',3,'Rohan Shelar',3,'SMC',13,'Healthcheck',NULL,'Application',2,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-08-05 02:34','2026-08-05 02:34:00','2026-08-05 06:34:00.000000','2026-08-05 02:44','2026-08-05 02:44:00','2026-08-05 06:44:00.000000','2026-08-05','EST','America/New_York',0,2,2,'2m','The Healthcheck project was found to be stuck, which caused the monitoring metrics to stop updating and triggered the alert. The Local Agent and Agent Connectors themselves were running normally and remained operational. We also observed that messages for one project were in a pending state.','We restarted the Healthcheck and affected project, which restored normal operation and resolved the alert.','By OC Team','00135666',NULL,'13m',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'10m',10,'2026-08-05 17:15:30','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(606,'INC-213','135696','Alert \'MESSRVPILOT - Critical Memory and Stagnant Request Alert [MESInsights - XPA]’ was fired','We have restarted the MES applications via the restart pipeline, and it has resolved the issue.','critical','closed',19,'Sushant Tadke',19,'NGC',3,'MES',NULL,'Application',2,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-08-08 18:49','2026-08-08 18:49:00','2026-08-08 13:19:00.000000','2026-08-08 19:31','2026-08-08 19:31:00','2026-08-08 14:01:00.000000','2026-08-08','IST','Asia/Kolkata',0,0,0,NULL,'None.','We have restarted the MES application using pipeline.','By OC Team','135696',NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'42m',42,'2026-08-08 14:55:42','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(607,'INC-214',NULL,'Christie Digital K8s- Pod Memory Utilization Exceeded 6 GB','We observed that the mosquitto-ccf5cfc9-kbhcd pod in the Christie Digital environment is consuming a high amount of memory over 6 GB.','critical','closed',3,'Rohan Shelar',3,'Christie Digital',12,'Local Agent',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-08-09 03:20','2026-08-09 03:20:00','2026-08-09 07:20:00.000000','2026-08-10 00:01','2026-08-10 00:01:00','2026-08-10 04:01:00.000000','2026-08-10','EST','America/New_York',0,0,0,NULL,'Local Agent mosquitto-ccf5cfc9-kbhcd pod was consuming memory beyond 6 GB due to cache memory.','Cloud team has reclaimed the cache memory which resolved the issue.','By Stakeholder','00135699',NULL,'10m',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-09 10:08:05','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(609,'INC-216',NULL,'Alert \'Free Disk Space Low’ was fired','Hi Team,\n\nWe have received an alert for free disk space low on NGCXPILAVM1.\n\nObservations:\nThere is low disk space for the C: drive on NGCXPILAVM1.\nCurrent free disk space is 15.2 GB.\n\nActions:\nWe ran Main_New.bat from %XPI_INSTALLATION%\\tool\\Main_New.bat.\nWe cleared the logs from below directory:\nC:\\Utils\\minio\\data\\temp\n\nCurrent Status: Alert has been resolved','critical','closed',11,'Balaji Karagir',11,'NGC',3,'NGC',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[\"@Rohan Shelar\"]',1,NULL,'2026-08-12 01:53','2026-08-12 01:53:00','2026-08-12 01:53:00.000000','2026-08-12 02:41','2026-08-12 02:41:00','2026-08-12 02:41:00.000000','2026-08-12','UTC','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'Disk full on C drive','We have cleared the space on c drive.','By OC Team','00135902',NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'48m',48,'2026-08-12 03:16:40','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(610,'INC-217',NULL,'NGC-Activated Severity: 0 MTH No Historian Read','Dear Customer,\n\n \nWe would like to inform you about a recent occurrence of a \'No Historian Read\' alert at MTH.\n\n- Plant Name: MTH\n\n- Incident Timestamp: August 11, 2026, 6:57 PM UTC\n\n- Duration: 40 minutes of plant is down.\n\n- Impact: Data is not flowing into FactoryEye for [MTH] while this alert is active.\n\nSteps Taken:\n\n We have identified that we were not reading data from the Historian server, and we are also unable to ping up the server.\n\nWe ask that someone on the NGC technical support team check the server’s network access, power to the server and/or the plant, the Historian licensing is active and lastly restart the server if all else fails.\n\nPlease inform us when you have a resolution to the issue, and/or you have verified that the server is operational.\n\nWe understand the importance of resolving this matter promptly, and we appreciate your collaboration towards ensuring a swift resolution.\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter.','critical','closed',11,'Balaji Karagir',11,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[\"@Abhishek Pawar\", \"@Rohan Shelar\"]',1,NULL,'2026-08-11 22:46','2026-08-11 22:46:00','2026-08-11 22:46:00.000000','2026-08-12 00:21','2026-08-12 00:21:00','2026-08-12 00:21:00.000000','2026-08-12','UTC','Etc/UTC',1,35,95,'1h 35m','Power outage at customer end.','Resolve by customer','By Customer','00135901',NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1h 35m',95,'2026-08-12 03:24:17','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(612,'INC-219',NULL,'NGC -Activated Severity: 0 Memory Usage','Hi Team,\n\n \n\nWe have received the critical alert for High Memory Usage over 90% on NGCXPILAVM1.\n\n \n\nDetails:\n\nTimestamp: 12, 2026 2:19 UTC.\n\nCustomer Name: National Gypsum Company (NGC)\n\n \n\nObservation:\n\nWe observed that memory consumption was high on NGCXPILAVM1.\n\nAfter analysing the memory consumption, file explorer and SAP project was consuming high memory.\n\n \n\nAfter Restarted SAP project alert was resolved.\n\n \n\nAction:\n\nWe have restarted the file explorer and SAP project.\n\n\nCurrent Status: The alert has been resolved.','critical','closed',11,'Balaji Karagir',11,'NGC',3,'NGC',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[\"@Rohan Shelar\"]',1,NULL,'2026-08-12 02:19','2026-08-12 02:19:00','2026-08-12 02:19:00.000000','2026-08-12 05:48','2026-08-12 05:48:00','2026-08-12 05:48:00.000000','2026-08-12','UTC','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'We observer that SAP project consuming high memory so we have restarted the project.','Restarted','By OC Team','00135900',NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'3h 29m',209,'2026-08-12 03:33:13','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(615,'INC-220','00135741','\'NGC - Azure: Activated Severity: 0 SHI No Historian Read','We have update from service desk due to SHI-APPSVR was undergoing scheduled security patching this alert was raised.','critical','closed',22,'Aatif Shaikh',22,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-08-13 08:14','2026-08-13 08:14:00','2026-08-13 08:14:00.000000','2026-08-13 09:03','2026-08-13 09:03:00','2026-08-13 09:03:00.000000','2026-08-13','UTC','Etc/UTC',0,49,49,'49m','We have update from service desk due to SHI-APPSVR was undergoing scheduled security patching this alert was raised.','Access was restored once security patching was completed.','By Customer','00135741',NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'2026-08-13 20:17:07','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(616,'INC-221',NULL,'Azure: Activated Severity: 0 ROT No Historian Read','The alert got auto-resolved.','critical','closed',14,'Mrunal Rajkar',14,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-08-14 05:19','2026-08-14 05:19:00','2026-08-13 23:49:00.000000','2026-08-14 05:45','2026-08-14 05:45:00','2026-08-14 00:15:00.000000','2026-08-14','IST','Asia/Kolkata',0,26,26,'26m','We received No Historian for Plant ROT, there was no response from service desk.\nThe alert got auto-resovled.',NULL,'By System','00135909',NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'26m',26,'2026-08-14 06:26:34','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(618,'INC-223',NULL,'Azure: Activated Severity: 0 BUR No Historian Read','We would like to inform you about a recent occurrence of a \'No Historian Read\' alert at BUR. \n\n- Plant Name: BUR\n- Incident Timestamp:  14Aug, 2026, 12:12 PM GMT\n- Duration: 60 Min\n- Impact: Data is not flowing into FactoryEye for BUR while this alert is active.\n\n\nWe have identified that we cannot read data from the Historian server. We ask that someone on the NGC technical support team check the server’s network access, power to the server and/or the plant, the Historian licensing is active and lastly, restart the server if all else fails.','critical','closed',2,'Babai Chatterjee',2,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-08-14 12:12','2026-08-14 12:12:00','2026-08-14 12:12:00.000000','2026-08-14 14:13','2026-08-14 14:13:00','2026-08-14 14:13:00.000000','2026-08-14','GMT','Etc/UTC',1,46,106,'1h 46m','No BUR Plant Data was flowing into factoryeye','The data automatically started','By System','00135912',NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2h 1m',121,'2026-08-14 13:13:37','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(619,'INC-224','00135746','Activated Severity: 0 CIN No Historian Read','Dear Team,\n\nWe would like to inform you about a recent occurrence of a \'No Historian Read\' alert at [CIN].\n\nPlease find the following details:\n\n- Plant Name: CIN [CIN-APPSVR]\n- \'No Historian Read\' Alert Details: [NGCXPILAVM1]\n- Incident Timestamp: August 16, 2026, 21:33 UTC.\n- Duration: 30 minutes plant is down.\n- Impact: Data is not flowing into Factory Eye for [CIN] while this alert is active.','critical','closed',28,'Anuja Bagadi',28,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-08-17 05:24','2026-08-17 05:24:00','2026-08-16 23:54:00.000000','2026-08-17 05:24','2026-08-17 05:24:00','2026-08-16 23:54:00.000000','2026-08-17','IST','Asia/Kolkata',0,0,0,NULL,'There is a power outage effecting the area due to weather.\nData has started flowing for CIN plant.\nThe alert has been resolved.','After Power Restoration, data has started flowing for CIN plant.','By Customer','00135746',NULL,'11m',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2h 21m',141,'2026-08-17 00:28:28','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(620,'INC-229',NULL,'Alert \'Redis Connection Lost’ was fired',NULL,'critical','closed',NULL,'Aatif Shaikh',2,'NGC',3,'Redis ','Redis ','Infrastructure',1,'Application',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'2026-06-03 02:37:00','2026-06-03 02:37:00',NULL,'2026-06-03 02:43:00','2026-06-03 02:43:00',NULL,'2026-06-03','IST','Asia/Kolkata',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'We have restarted the \'ngcdigitaltwin\' service and executed the required commands, which resolved the alert.',NULL,'00135147','Yes',NULL,5,'Jun\'26','Support-HQ','Closed',NULL,'Cloud Incidents from Jun\'26 to Jul\'26.xlsx','{\"values\": {\"Area\": \"Infrastructure\", \"Month\": \"Jun\'26\", \"Subject\": \"Alert \'Redis Connection Lost’ was fired\", \"Customer\": \"NGC\", \"Severity\": \"Normal\", \"Resolution\": \"We have restarted the \'ngcdigitaltwin\' service and executed the required commands, which resolved the alert.\", \"case_owner\": \"Aatif Shaikh\", \"sf_case_no\": \"00135147\", \"Closed Date\": \"2026-06-03\", \"R&D Tickets\": \"\", \"Account Name\": \"Support-HQ\", \"Project Area\": \"Redis \", \"product_line\": \"Application\", \"Downtime(Mins)\": \"0\", \"Internal Status\": \"Closed\", \"Date/Time Closed\": \"2026-06-03 02:43:00\", \"Date/Time Opened\": \"2026-06-03 02:37:00\", \"Incident Report status\": \"Yes\", \"Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)\": \"5\"}, \"source_row\": 2, \"excel_serials\": {\"Closed Date\": \"46176\", \"Date/Time Closed\": \"46176.113194444442\", \"Date/Time Opened\": \"46176.109027777777\"}, \"source_sha256\": \"e1b96eac153502b4612d23e4e5de6f2048f9d33f2626ba55ac75bf8cc5683d02\"}',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-18 10:51:47','2026-09-28 13:44:20'),(621,'INC-230',NULL