nds. After that, we tested the APIs to verify whether Redis was working as expected. However, the APIs were not returning any data, so we further stopped and restarted the <strong>ngcfactoryeyeapiv3</strong> App Service. Once the App Service was restarted, we tested the APIs again and confirmed that the expected response was being received.','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'27m',27,'2026-09-25 05:36:53','2026-09-29 09:48:31'),(772,'INC-332',NULL,'Alert \'MagicXPA_InactiveProjectsAlert’ was fired','Alert \'MagicXPA_InactiveProjectsAlert’ was fired','critical','closed',2,'Babai Chatterjee',2,'NGC',3,'NGCGYP',NULL,'NGC - MDE',20,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-09-25 06:02','2026-09-25 06:02:00','2026-09-25 06:02:00.000000','2026-09-25 06:17','2026-09-25 06:17:00','2026-09-25 06:17:00.000000','2026-09-25','GMT','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'There were possibility thst the matrics which is responsible for checking the project running status were failed or delayed for fe min, due to that alert raised.','After restarting the broker service the alert got resolved','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'15m',15,'2026-09-25 06:19:46','2026-09-29 09:48:03'),(773,'INC-333',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / Toridoll- Average K8s Node Memory Utilization Higher than 80%','We\'ve detected that the query has exceeded 80 for over 100% of the following','critical','closed',2,'Babai Chatterjee',2,'TORIDOLL',20,'NodeMemory',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-09-25 19:01','2026-09-25 19:01:00','2026-09-25 10:01:00.000000','2026-09-25 21:34','2026-09-25 21:34:00','2026-09-25 12:34:00.000000','2026-09-25','JST','Asia/Tokyo',0,0,0,NULL,'Due to Multiple project pod consuming more than 1.5GB','After redeploying the projects it resolved the alert','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2h 33m',153,'2026-09-25 10:16:12','2026-09-29 09:47:25'),(775,'INC-335',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / To