"2026-10-01T10:25:06.142Z\"}]','2026-09-30 15:00','2026-09-30 15:00:00','2026-09-30 15:00:00.000000','2026-09-30 15:41','2026-09-30 15:41:00','2026-09-30 15:41:00.000000','2026-09-30','GMT','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'There was latency observed in application insights service which caused missing metrics which triggered this alert. However, all the xpi applications were up and running.','Alert was auto resolved after some time.','By System',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'41m',41,'2026-09-30 15:20:22','2026-10-01 11:24:15');
INSERT INTO `incidents` VALUES (784,'INC-343',NULL,'Azure: Activated Severity: 0 BUR No Historian Read','Dear Team,<br><br>We would like to inform you about a recent occurrence of a \'No Historian Read\' alert at BUR.<br>Our team has conducted an investigation and prepared a detailed report to provide you with all the necessary information.<br><br>Please find the following details:<br><br>- Plant Name: BUR[BUR-APPSVR]<br>- \'No Historian Read\' Alert Details: [NGCXPILAVM1]<br><br>- Duration: [insert the time here] minutes plant BUR is down.<br>- Impact: Data is not flowing into FactoryEye for BUR while this alert is active.<br><br>Please find attached a screenshot for your reference.<br><br><br><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"image.png\"><br><br><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"image.png\"><br><br><br>- Steps Taken:<br><br>We have identified that we were not reading data from the Historian server and are not able to ping.<br>We have identified that we cannot read data from the Historian server. We ask that someone on the NGC technical support team check the server’s network access, power to the server and/or the plant, the Historian licensing is active and lastly restart the server if all else fails.<br>Please inform us when you have a resolution to the issue, and/or you have verified that the server is operational.<br>We understand the importance of resolving this matter promptly, and we appreciate your collaboration towards ensuring a swift resolution.<br><br>Thank you for your attention to this matter.','critical','closed',18,'Shantanu Patil',18,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,'[{\"type\": \"comment\", \"action\": \"commented\", \"author\": \"Rohan Shelar\", \"detail\": \"Hi @Pooja Thakkhi , have you tried to reach ServiceDesk via phone call? Issue still persists and we did not get any update from customer/ServiceDesk.\", \"author_id\": 3, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-01T11:45:44.109Z\"}]','2026-09-30 21:44','2026-09-30 21:44:00','2026-09-30 21:44:00.000000','2026-10-01 17:53','2026-10-01 17:53:00','2026-10-01 17:53:00.000000','2026-10-01','GMT','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'We have not received any update from the Service Desk regarding the reason why this alert was raised. Also, the BUR plant was running as per the weekend schedule.','The alert got resolved automatically&nbsp;','By System',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'20h 9m',1209,'2026-09-30 21:54:41','2026-10-01 17:57:22'),(785,'INC-344',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / Toridoll- Average K8s Node Memory Utilization Higher than 80%','We\'ve detected that the query has exceeded 80 for over 100% of the following','critical','closed',3,'Rohan Shelar',3,'TORIDOLL',20,'Node Memory',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-01 17:34','2026-10-01 17:34:00','2026-10-01 08:34:00.000000','2026-10-02 06:49','2026-10-02 06:49:00','2026-10-01 21:49:00.000000','2026-10-02','JST','Asia/Tokyo',0,0,0,NULL,'Due to larger amount of memory consumptions of multiple project pods(more than 1.5 GB each)','By redeplpying the projects it resolved the alert','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'15m',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'13h 15m',795,'2026-10-01 08:53:09','2026-10-02 05:09:36'),(786,'INC-345',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / Toridoll- K8s- Pod Memory Utilization Exceeded 6GB','We\'ve detected that the query has exceeded 0 for over 0% of the following','critical','closed',18,'Shantanu Patil',18,'TORIDOLL',20,'M0118_Salesforce_to_DMP_Yext',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,'[{\"type\": \"comment\", \"action\": \"commented\", \"author\": \"Babai Chatterjee\", \"detail\": \"@Shantanu Patil Please monitor this project pod status further\", \"author_id\": 2, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-02T14:19:49.899Z\"}]','2026-10-02 05:44','2026-10-02 05:44:00','2026-10-01 20:44:00.000000','2026-10-02 06:58','2026-10-02 06:58:00','2026-10-01 21:58:00.000000','2026-10-02','JST','Asia/Tokyo',0,0,0,NULL,'<div>The memory growth came from one scheduled request stuck on one step:</div><div><br></div><div>Message ID 444380, triggered by the Scheduler at 05:10 JST (Server ID 257, Worker 36239), status IN_PROCESS</div><div><br></div><div>The worker stopped at step [5-18-17-2. メイン処理], inside sub-flow sub_YEXT取得 (Yext data retrieval, step \"ファイルblob作成\", file blob creation)</div><div><br></div><div>No activity after 05:21:56 JST, but the message stayed IN_PROCESS and memory kept growing</div><div><br></div><div>The Coralogix alert fired at 05:44 JST, about 30 minutes after the scheduled run started</div><div><br></div><div>The flow was most likely holding the retrieved Yext data in memory (BLOB) without releasing it. The project has no memory limit, so nothing stopped it before it threatened the whole node.</div>','The issue was resolved by restarting the M0118_Salesforce_to_DMP_Yext project, which released approximately 13 GB of memory utilization.','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1h 14m',74,'2026-10-01 20:58:31','2026-10-02 14:19:49'),(787,'INC-346',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / Christie Digital K8s- Pod Memory Utilization Exceeded 6 GB','We\'ve detected that the query has exceeded 6442450944 for over 0% of the following','critical','closed',20,'Vibha Khanke',20,'Christie Digital',12,'mosquitto',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-01 19:34','2026-10-01 19:34:00','2026-10-01 23:34:00.000000','2026-10-01 20:21','2026-10-01 20:21:00','2026-10-02 00:21:00.000000','2026-10-01','EST','America/New_York',0,0,0,NULL,'Local Agent&nbsp;<font>mosquitto-5c98767cbc-swj24&nbsp;</font>pod was consuming memory beyond 6 GB due to cache memory.','Cloud team has reclaimed the cache memory which resolved the issue.','By Stakeholder',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'47m',47,'2026-10-01 23:52:59','2026-10-05 06:32:17'),(789,'INC-347',NULL,'Alert \'MESSRVPILOT - Critical Memory and Stagnant Request Alert [MESInsights - XPA]’ was fired','Alert \'MESSRVPILOT - Critical Memory and Stagnant Request Alert [MESInsights - XPA]’ was fired','critical','closed',19,'Sushant Tadke',19,'NGC',3,'MESSRVPILOT',NULL,'NGC - MES',21,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-03 07:04','2026-10-03 07:04:00','2026-10-03 07:04:00.000000','2026-10-03 07:34','2026-10-03 07:34:00','2026-10-03 07:34:00.000000','2026-10-03','GMT','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'High&nbsp;Memory and Stagnant Request, we have received Critical Alert for MESSRVPILOT.','We have restarted the MES application using pipeline. Currently the application is up and running&nbsp;and The alert is resolved.','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'3m',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'30m',30,'2026-10-03 07:14:07','2026-10-03 07:39:21'),(791,'INC-349',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / Christie Digital_EC2 Low Free Disk Space','We\'ve detected that the query was equal or exceeded 90 for over 0% of the following','critical','closed',20,'Vibha Khanke',20,'Christie Digital',12,'EC2 Disk',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,'[{\"type\": \"comment\", \"action\": \"commented\", \"author\": \"Shantanu Patil\", \"detail\": \"@Babai Chatterjee we need to automate this cleanup activity\", \"author_id\": 18, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-06T07:43:41.598Z\"}]','2026-10-04 18:03','2026-10-04 18:03:00','2026-10-04 22:03:00.000000','2026-10-04 18:29','2026-10-04 18:29:00','2026-10-04 22:29:00.000000','2026-10-04','EST','America/New_York',0,0,0,NULL,'<span style=\"background-color: rgb(245, 246, 250);\">Due to disk space consumed above 90%</span>','<span style=\"background-color: rgb(245, 246, 250);\">We have cleared the Runtime logs</span>','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'3m',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'26m',26,'2026-10-04 22:52:29','2026-10-19 12:30:22'),(792,'INC-350',NULL,'Azure: Activated Severity: 0 JSP No Historian Read','Dear Team,<br><br>We would like to inform you about a recent occurrence of a \'No Historian Read\' alert at JSP.<br>Our team has conducted an investigation and prepared a detailed report to provide you with all the necessary information.<br><br>Please find the following details:<br><br>- Plant Name: JSP[JSP-APPSVR]<br>- \'No Historian Read\' Alert Details: [NGCXPILAVM1]<br><br>- Duration: [insert the time here] minutes plant JSP is down.<br>- Impact: Data is not flowing into FactoryEye for JSP while this alert is active.<br><br>Please find attached a screenshot for your reference.<br><br><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"image.png\"><br><br><br>- Steps Taken:<br><br>We have identified that we were not reading data from the Historian server and are not able to ping.<br>We have identified that we cannot read data from the Historian server. We ask that someone on the NGC technical support team check the server’s network access, power to the server and/or the plant, the Historian licensing is active and lastly restart the server if all else fails.<br>Please inform us when you have a resolution to the issue, and/or you have verified that the server is operational.<br>We understand the importance of resolving this matter promptly, and we appreciate your collaboration towards ensuring a swift resolution.<br><br>Thank you for your attention to this matter.','critical','closed',20,'Vibha Khanke',20,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-05 01:10','2026-10-05 01:10:00','2026-10-05 01:10:00.000000','2026-10-05 01:38','2026-10-05 01:38:00','2026-10-05 01:38:00.000000','2026-10-05','GMT','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'The alert got resolved automatically.','The alert got resolved automatically.','By System',NULL,NULL,'3m',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'28m',28,'2026-10-05 01:22:12','2026-10-05 01:39:34'),(794,'INC-352',NULL,'Alert \'Free Disk Space Low’ was fired','<div>Hi Team,</div><div><br></div><div>We have received an alert for free disk space low on NGCXPAPRODVM1.</div><div><br></div><div>Observations:</div><div>There is low disk space for the C: drive on NGCXPAPRODVM1.</div><div><br></div><div>Actions:</div><div>We have purged the MySQL binary log files</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Current Status: Alert has been resolved</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you.</div><div>Best Regards,</div><div><br></div>','critical','closed',28,'Anuja Bagadi',28,'NGC',3,'NGC',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-06 02:21','2026-10-06 02:21:00','2026-10-05 20:51:00.000000','2026-10-06 02:41','2026-10-06 02:41:00','2026-10-05 21:11:00.000000','2026-10-06','IST','Asia/Kolkata',0,0,0,NULL,'<div>There is low disk space for the C: drive on NGCXPAPRODVM1.</div><div><br></div>','<div>We have purged the MySQL binary log files.</div><div><span style=\"color: var(--text); font-family: inherit;\">&nbsp;Alert has been resolved</span></div><div><br></div>','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'20m',20,'2026-10-05 21:20:46','2026-10-19 12:30:22'),(795,'INC-353',NULL,'Alert \'Critical Alert - MDE Health Status Inactive’ was fired','<div>Hello Team,</div><div><br></div><div>We have received \'Critical Alert - MDE Health Status Inactive’ was fired</div><div><br></div><div>Machine Name: NGCXPAVM1</div><div>Application Name: NGCGYP<br><br><div>Details:</div><div>Timestamp: 06-10-2026 09:11 AM IST</div><div>Customer Name: National Gypsum Company (NGC)</div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div>','critical','closed',20,'Vibha Khanke',20,'NGC',3,'MDE',NULL,'NGC - MDE',20,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-06 03:41','2026-10-06 03:41:00','2026-10-06 03:41:00.000000','2026-10-06 05:27','2026-10-06 05:27:00','2026-10-06 05:27:00.000000','2026-10-06','GMT','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'<!--StartFragment-->We observed that the NGC dashboard and the NGCGYPV01 application were showing an Inactive status.However, the health status URL for NGCGYPV01 was showing as:<!--EndFragment-->','<div>We observed a “No more licenses available” error for the NGCGYP application.</div><div>We added another instance of the NGCGYP application.</div>','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1h 46m',106,'2026-10-06 05:36:39','2026-10-19 12:30:22'),(796,'INC-354',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / Christie Digital_EC2 Low Free Disk Space','We\'ve detected that the query was equal or exceeded 90 for over 0% of the following','critical','closed',3,'Rohan Shelar',3,'Christie Digital',12,'EC2 Disk',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-07 03:16','2026-10-07 03:16:00','2026-10-07 07:16:00.000000','2026-10-07 03:42','2026-10-07 03:42:00','2026-10-07 07:42:00.000000','2026-10-07','EST','America/New_York',0,0,0,NULL,'There is low disk space for the C: Drive on Christie Digital Production EC2 environment. When investigated we observed that xpi logs were consuming almost 10 GB of disk space from following directory - C:\\xpi\\xpi4141\\Runtime\\Logs\\java','<div>We executed the log cleanup batch file which cleared logs from the following directory C:\\xpi\\xpi4141\\Runtime\\Logs\\java.&nbsp;The current free space is 18.0 GB.</div>','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'11m',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'26m',26,'2026-10-07 07:27:16','2026-10-07 07:43:02'),(797,'INC-355',NULL,'Azure: Activated Severity: 2 CPU Usage','Azure: Activated Severity: 2 CPU Usage<div><br><div><div>Hello team,</div><div><br></div><div>We have received the alert for High CPU Usage triggered for \"virtualMachines/NGCXPAVM1\".</div></div><div><br><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"image.png\"><br><br></div></div>','critical','closed',8,'Aniruddh Potdar',8,'NGC',3,'virtualMachines/NGCXPAVM1',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-08 10:18','2026-10-08 10:18:00','2026-10-08 04:48:00.000000','2026-10-08 10:58','2026-10-08 10:58:00','2026-10-08 05:28:00.000000','2026-10-08','IST','Asia/Kolkata',0,0,0,NULL,'<div data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\" style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">The NGCCB project, which was consuming High CPU and High Memory.</div><div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\"><br style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36); font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Web (West European)&quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"></div>','<div data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\" style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">We have restarted the NGCCB project, which was consuming High CPU and High Memory.</div><div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\">After this, the alert is now resolved.</div><div style=\"border: 0px; font: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit;\"><br style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36); font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Web (West European)&quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"></div>','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'40m',40,'2026-10-08 05:13:04','2026-10-19 12:30:22'),(798,'INC-356',NULL,'Alert \'Redis Container Instance Restarted’ was fired','Alert \'Redis Container Instance Restarted’ was fired','critical','closed',2,'Babai Chatterjee',2,'NGC',3,'Redis',NULL,'Redis',10,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-09 10:02','2026-10-09 10:02:00','2026-10-09 10:02:00.000000','2026-10-09 10:43','2026-10-09 10:43:00','2026-10-09 10:43:00.000000','2026-10-09','GMT','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'Due to the Redis restart, fresh connections were established, but the API remained stuck on the old connections.','After the restart, the API established a fresh connection and started receiving responses successfully.','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'41m',41,'2026-10-09 10:14:29','2026-10-09 10:43:52'),(799,'INC-357',NULL,'Azure: Activated Severity: 0 DLS No Historian Read','Dear Team,<br><br>We would like to inform you about a recent occurrence of a \'No Historian Read\' alert at DLS.<br>Our team has conducted an investigation and prepared a detailed report to provide you with all the necessary information.<br><br>Please find the following details:<br><br>- Plant Name: DLS[DLS-APPSVR]<br>- \'No Historian Read\' Alert Details: [NGCXPILAVM1]<br><br>- Duration: 40 minutes plant DLS is down.<br>- Impact: Data is not flowing into FactoryEye for DLS while this alert is active.<br><br><br><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"image.png\"><br><br>- Steps Taken:<br><br>We have identified that we were not reading data from the Historian server and are not able to ping.<br>We have identified that we cannot read data from the Historian server. We ask that someone on the NGC technical support team check the server’s network access, power to the server and/or the plant, the Historian licensing is active and lastly restart the server if all else fails.<br>Please inform us when you have a resolution to the issue, and/or you have verified that the server is operational.<br>We understand the importance of resolving this matter promptly, and we appreciate your collaboration towards ensuring a swift resolution.<br><br>Thank you for your attention to this matter.','critical','closed',19,'Sushant Tadke',19,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'FactoryEye',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-10 06:54','2026-10-10 06:54:00','2026-10-10 06:54:00.000000','2026-10-12 09:03','2026-10-12 09:03:00','2026-10-12 09:03:00.000000','2026-10-12','GMT','Etc/UTC',50,0,3000,'50h','Plant was down for maintenance activities.','Plant resumed the normal operations which resolved the issue.','By Stakeholder',NULL,NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'50h 9m',3009,'2026-10-10 07:10:22','2026-10-12 12:55:46'),(800,'INC-358',NULL,'Azure Monitor alert activated for your availability test, aiml - node-ngcmdeapp, with severity 0','Azure Monitor alert activated for your availability test, aiml - node-ngcmdeapp, with severity 0','critical','closed',19,'Sushant Tadke',19,'NGC',3,'AIML',NULL,'NGC - AIML',19,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-10 07:12','2026-10-10 07:12:00','2026-10-10 07:12:00.000000','2026-10-10 07:43','2026-10-10 07:43:00','2026-10-10 07:43:00.000000','2026-10-10','GMT','Etc/UTC',0,0,0,NULL,'<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;\nmso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:\nEN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">due to the scheduled\nmaintenance of Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server instance\nngcaimlanomalydatabase,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;\nmso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:\nEN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">database connection\nloss with AIML Dashboard application.</span>','<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;\nmso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:\nEN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">We have restarted the\n\'ngcaimldashboard\' app service using application restart pipeline and it\nresolved the issue.<br>\n<!--[if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br>\n<!--[endif]--></span>','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'31m',31,'2026-10-10 07:25:30','2026-10-10 07:45:11'),(801,'INC-359',NULL,'Alert \'MESSRVPILOT - Critical Memory and Stagnant Request Alert [MESInsights - XPA]’ was fired','Alert \'MESSRVPILOT - Critical Memory and Stagnant Request Alert [MESInsights - XPA]’ was fired','critical','closed',14,'Mrunal Rajkar',14,'NGC',3,'MES Application',NULL,'NGC - MES',21,'Application',NULL,NULL,'[]',1,NULL,'2026-10-10 19:23','2026-10-10 19:23:00','2026-10-10 13:53:00.000000','2026-10-10 19:39','2026-10-10 19:39:00','2026-10-10 14:09:00.000000','2026-10-10','IST','As