 - fails with status \"inactive\"’ was state::2026-10-14','This alert was triggered due to NGC monthly maintenance. Rest all alerts were disabled prior to activity except for this alert.',0,3,'2026-10-14 12:23:19'),(68,'4d6989c41e765d206ac04ac19926c138d3f9e4573a29c1c2acbaee49e7af81e3','azure-noreply@microsoft.com::important notice: azure monitor alert ngc resource health alert rule was state::2026-10-14','This alert was triggered due to NGC monthly maintenance. Rest all alerts were disabled prior to activity except for this alert.',0,3,'2026-10-14 12:23:39'),(69,'e4cbc10075a01cac50ab3766a39e407285afe021566e9672302807dde767485c','alerts@coralogix.com::coralogix alert on magic / toridoll- project status down for more than 5mins.::2026-10-14','After redeployment of the project, the alert is resolved, and it was snoozed for mean time.',1,8,'2026-10-14 12:37:43'),(70,'4d6989c41e765d206ac04ac19926c138d3f9e4573a29c1c2acbaee49e7af81e3','azure-noreply@microsoft.com::important notice: azure monitor alert ngc resource health alert rule was state::2026-10-14','Marked as resolved (no comment provided)',1,8,'2026-10-14 12:40:22'),(71,'9a2cc324b812a8bb91936d865c5bbd79814894a6aff721327ab2aa0a1707afee','alerts@coralogix.com::coralogix alert on magic / matrix - average k8s node memory utilization higher than 80%::2026-10-14','Auto resolved',0,8,'2026-10-14 12:40:54'),(72,'9a2cc324b812a8bb91936d865c5bbd79814894a6aff721327ab2aa0a1707afee','alerts@coralogix.com::coralogix alert on magic / matrix - average k8s node memory utilization higher than 80%::2026-10-14','We have snoozed the alert for now is its repeatadly occuring. CSO will check on the memory release',0,2,'2026-10-14 15:55:48'),(73,'9b06dc9ec751804dbe2e1d5280f84bca283a3e6e437f3b8678a9a8b5681b5d3e','azure-noreply@microsoft.com::important notice: azure monitor alert ngc resource health alert rule was state::2026-10-15','This is a false alarm. We confirmed that VM was up and running. Alert was triggered due to network latency in application insights.',0,3,'2026-10-15 16:09:43'),(74,'9b06dc9ec751804dbe2e1d5280f84bca283a3e6e437f3b8678a9a8b5681b5d3e','azure-noreply@microsoft.com::important notice: azure monitor alert ngc resource health alert rule was state::2026-10-15','Marked as resolved (no comment provided)',1,3,'2026-10-15 16:09:55'),(75,'c6bb8ca377c3890431642330445febb5d17ca3d65886bf508ea1444b05147b23','jira::TOR-307','We have analysed the project logs and checked the database settings.\n\nOur findings are below:\n\nWhat happened\nThe errors occurred between 11:23:52 and 11:24:02, during the step that inserts employee records into the database (step ID 4).\nAt 11:23:52, the database closed an open connection (\"Communications link failure\").\nFor the next 9 records, the database refused new connections. The Activity Log shows these as \"General Error - Result State is false\". The detailed project log shows the actual error returned by the database: \"Out of memory; check if mysqld or some other process uses all available memory\".\nFrom 11:24:03, all database operations succeeded again, and the 12:00 and later runs completed without errors.',0,2,'2026-10-17 19:27:15'),(76,'c6bb8ca377c3890431642330445febb5d17ca3d65886bf508ea1444b05147b23','jira::TOR-307','Possible root cause-\nA short memory shortage on the AWS RDS Aurora instance at around 11:23:52. During this time it closed one active connection and refused new connections until it recovered at about 11:24:03.\nThe database settings (maximum 90 connections, with a peak of 75 recorded) suggest a relatively small instance. The instance is also shared with other workloads, so the memory demand may not have come only from this project.\nWe are confirming this with our cloud team using the AWS monitoring data.',0,2,'2026-10-17 19:27:36'),(77,'5ec045374cbea44fe1e4fd33a8a9000d659a9dd6bf6851fe0a23642cabe7c378','alerts@coralogix.com::coralogix alert on magic / toridoll- average k8s node memory utilization higher than 80%::2026-10-18','This is 